# The boxes demo at 640x400 CSS px at 1x. The card is at x 30..204,
# y 108..222 with a shadow below; the four-colour box at x 228..408,
# y 108..228; the buttons sit at y about 256..292.
pixel 4 4 #e9ecef          page, top left
pixel 100 205 #ffffff      the card's fill, below its text
pixel 318 109 #d32f2f      the four-colour box: top border, red
pixel 406 170 #388e3c      right border, green
pixel 318 226 #1976d2      bottom border, blue
pixel 229 170 #fbc02d      left border, yellow
pixel 300 180 #ffffff      inside it, white
pixel 186 260 #3a7bd5      the primary button's fill
pixel 184 273 #2f63ad      its 1px border
ink 60 222 180 236 #e9ecef the card's shadow darkens the page below it

# A phone's width (Tom's, 412 CSS px): the cards wrap two to a row, so
# the first card lies on screen at x 17..191, y 237..351. As one row
# that does not wrap, it would sit at x -79..95, and the gpu tier's
# check at x 100 fails (proven by removing flex-wrap).
at 412x800
pixel 18 340 #ffffff       the first card, one pixel in from its left edge
pixel 100 340 #ffffff      the first card's fill, past where an unwrapped row ends it
pixel 185 340 #ffffff      the first card's fill near its right edge
